// =====================================================================================
// Ingest: intellectual sources on interpreting ACRs, and four principles grounded in them.
// Prepared 2026-10-17 for Daniel Fontaine from the ACR research in
// app/database/ontology/impact-matrix/acr-interpretation-research.md.
// GENERATED by a scratch builder (build_acr_batch.py). Re-run the builder rather than editing.
//
// RECON (2026-10-17)
//   - IntellectualSource is unique on name and unique_id. Principle is unique on handle and
//     unique_id. derives_from and contested_by carry provision, quote, rationale,
//     assessed_date; derives_from also carries grounding_kind.
//   - None of the sources below exists as an IntellectualSource. Already in the graph and
//     not re-created: Harvard "How to Interpret a VPAT", the Massachusetts ACR checklist,
//     the ITI VPAT page, VPAT 2.5Rev, the GSA ACR Supplement (Guideline 75f09ff5...).
//   - Four sources already exist as IntellectualSources and are matched by their existing
//     name, so MERGE adds only the new edges and leaves their properties unchanged:
//     Michigan "Evaluate Compliance Documentation", Falloon and O'Reilly "Prioritizing
//     Accessibility in the E-Resources Procurement Lifecycle", Brajnik et al. 2010, and
//     "Brajnik, Barrier Walkthrough" (standing in for the 2008 WISE paper on the method).
//   - Two GSA pages already exist as Webpages. The new IntellectualSources for them link
//     to those Webpages with is_sourced_from (6e19ac91..., 9807d32a...).
//   - principle:vendor-claims-require-proportionate-validation is already named by
//     EVIDENCE_LIMITS.grounds in review-matrix.js but had no node. This creates it.
//
// JUDGMENT CALLS
//   - 42 source rows (38 new, 4 existing). Left out: campus pages of the SFBRN campuses (those are implementations),
//     a commercial grading tool (a vendor's description of its own offering), and sources
//     read only secondhand (Mune and Agee, Alonso et al., Harrison and Petrie).
//   - grounding_kind: scholarship for peer-reviewed and journal work; interpretation for
//     government, institutional and practitioner guidance, which reads the standard but
//     binds no one. One edge to the GSA ACR Supplement Guideline, also interpretation.
//   - Quotes come from pages fetched during the research. Only the three GSA quotes were
//     checked against stored raw_text. The other sources have no raw_text yet; capture it
//     with /get-source-text. Edges read from an abstract say so in their rationale.
//   - Commercial bias is stated in description_full for sources that sell VPAT services.
//   - contested_by: two university rubrics and Tarnoff's page-share rule, which read
//     severity from the count of conformance labels.
//
// NOT DONE
//   - shapes edges for the four principles. Separate pass.
//   - raw_text capture. Run /get-source-text on these sources.
//
// VALIDATE FIRST
//   python -m app.database.cypher_runner.run_file app/database/batch/auto-assignments/ingest_2026_10_17_acr_interpretation_sources.cypher
//   python -m app.database.cypher_runner.run_file app/database/batch/auto-assignments/ingest_2026_10_17_acr_interpretation_sources.cypher --execute
